    "q-85393": {
      "dom_id": "step-q85393",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "Which of the following numbers are divisible by $3?$\n\nI. $896\\,154$\n\nII. $12\\,471\\,106$\n\nIII. $3\\,472\\,335$",
      "worked_solution": "A number is divisible by $3$ if the sum of its digits is divisible by $3.$\n\n- The sum of the digits of $896\\,154$ is\n\n$$\n8+9+6+1+5+4=33,\n$$\n\nwhich is divisible by $3.$ So, $896\\,154$ is divisible by $3.$\n\n- The sum of the digits of $12\\,471\\,106$ is\n\n$$\n1+2+4+7+1+1+0+6=22,\n$$\n\nwhich is *not* divisible by $3.$ So, $12\\,471\\,106$ is *not* divisible by $3.$\n\n- The sum of the digits of $3\\,472\\,335$ is\n\n$$\n3+4+7+2+3+3+5=27,\n$$\n\nwhich is divisible by $3.$ So, $3\\,472\\,335$ is divisible by $3.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
