    "q-85144": {
      "dom_id": "step-q85144",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "Which digits, when inserted into the blank, make the number $173\\,◻32\\,338$ divisible by $9?$\n\nI. $4$\n\nII. $6$\n\nIII. $9$",
      "worked_solution": "A number is divisible by $9$ if the sum of its digits is divisible by $9.$\n\nFor the number $173\\,◻32\\,338\\,$ the sum of the digits is\n\n$$\n1+7+3+◻+3+2+3+3+8=30+◻.\n$$\n\nNow, let's consider each of the given digits that could be inserted into the blank.\n\n- If we insert $4$ into the blank, then the sum of the digits is $30+4=34,$ which is *not* divisible by $9.$\n\n- If we insert $6$ into the blank, then the sum of the digits is $30+6=36,$ which is divisible by $9.$\n\n- If we insert $9$ into the blank, then the sum of the digits is $30+9=39,$ which is *not* divisible by $9.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"",
