    "q-132408": {
      "dom_id": "step-q132408",
      "name": "Question 6",
      "problem": "Which of the following numbers are divisible by $6?$\n\nI. $345\\,989\\,191$\n\nII. $55\\,355\\,676$\n\nIII. $137\\,252\\,124$",
      "worked_solution": "A number is divisible by $6$ if it is divisible by both $2$ and $3.$\n\n- The number $345\\,989\\,191$ is not divisible by $2,$ so it is not divisible by $6.$\n\n- The number $55\\,355\\,676$ is divisible by $2,$ and it is also divisible by $3$ since the sum of its digits is divisible by $3:$\n\n$$\n5+5+3+5+5+6+7+6=42\n$$\n\nSo, $55\\,355\\,676$ is divisible by $6.$\n\n- The number $137\\,252\\,124$ is divisible by $2,$ and it is also divisible by $3$ since the sum of its digits is divisible by $3:$\n\n$$\n1+3+7+2+5+2+1+2+4=27\n$$\n\nSo, $137\\,252\\,124$ is divisible by $6.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
