    "q-132405": {
      "dom_id": "step-q132405",
      "name": "Question 9",
      "problem": "Which of the following numbers are divisible by $6?$\n\nI. $185\\,346$\n\nII. $2\\,525\\,934$\n\nIII. $15\\,070\\,962$",
      "worked_solution": "A number is divisible by $6$ if it is divisible by both $2$ and $3.$\n\n- The number $185\\,346$ is divisible by $2,$ and it is also divisible by $3$ since the sum of its digits is divisible by $3:$\n\n$$\n1+8+5+3+4+6=27\n$$\n\nSo, $185\\,346$ is divisible by $6.$\n\n- The number $2\\,525\\,934$ is divisible by $2,$ and it is also divisible by $3$ since the sum of its digits is divisible by $3:$\n\n$$\n2+5+2+5+9+3+4=30\n$$\n\nSo, $2\\,525\\,934$ is divisible by $6.$\n\n- The number $15\\,070\\,962$ is divisible by $2,$ and it is also divisible by $3$ since the sum of its digits is divisible by $3:$\n\n$$\n1+5+0+7+0+9+6+2=30\n$$\n\nSo, $15\\,070\\,962$ is divisible by $6.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\"",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
