    "q-223369": {
      "dom_id": "step-q223369",
      "name": "Question 13",
      "problem": "Which of the following numbers are divisible by $7?$\n\nI. $447$\n\nII. $406$\n\nIII. $847$",
      "worked_solution": "To check if a number is divisible by $7,$ double the last digit, subtract the result from the remaining digits, and then check if the difference is divisible by $7.$\n\n- For the number $447,$ we have that \n\n$$\n44-2(7)=44-14=30\n$$\n\nwhich is not divisible by $7.$ Therefore, $447$ is not divisible by $7.$\n\n- For the number $406,$ we have that \n\n$$\n40-2(6)=40-12=28\n$$\n\nwhich is divisible by $7.$ Therefore, $406$ is divisible by $7.$\n\n- For the number $847,$ we have that \n\n$$\n84-2(7)=84-14=70\n$$\n\nwhich is divisible by $7.$ Therefore, $847$ is divisible by $7.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
